+## [1784461767] p-min/contract
+- Situation: Writing the one-page CONTRACT.md from EXPERIMENT-BRIEF.md for a downstream implementer.
+- Options: (1) restate all 19 criteria; (2) write only the delta — sharpenings, prohibitions, exact formats, verbatim constants.
+- Decision: Wrote delta-only; the implementer shares the worktree and reads the brief. Promoted every code trap (Selector::parse("&") errors; non-dense idx on both old-resolve and new-match sides; idx-derived numbers in messages; abort-before-tx; None/Some("") author key; token-both-or-none) into prohibition lines.
+- Why: The task caps the contract at 60 lines and demands criteria not warnings; delta form fits budget and every trap is assertable.
+- Spec-gap: B step-2 precedence ("highest-precedence rule wins") was ambiguous between per-chapter-any-rule and global-tier priority. Resolved in favor of global tier priority a>b>c with smallest-idx tiebreak in a single ascending pass. B6 message format left "free" by brief — pinned to exact clauses (進度已遷移：{name} / 進度重置到首章) to make it assertable and to forbid the latent idx+1 bug.
+
+## [1784462400] p-min/impl
+- Situation: Item A — `Selector::parse(&alt.selector)` ran unconditionally before the `alt.selector == "&"` check in `extract_within`, and `select_nodes`/`select_within`/`extract_doc`/`extract_all_doc` had no self-branch at all (document-level `&` was simply broken, not just extract_within).
