+- Decision: (2) — added the pre-parse guard to `select_nodes`, `select_within`, `extract_doc`, `extract_within`, `extract_all_doc`. Never call `Selector::parse("&")` on any path.
+- Why: Contract explicitly required the guard in all five entry points and forbade `Selector::parse("&")` anywhere; A7 was listed as in-scope for this contract (not marked skip).
+- Spec-gap: none — A1-A7 all directly covered by pinning tests exercising the real fn signatures.
+
+- Situation: Item B — the dao's `update_book_source_tx` always resets `progress.chapter_index` to `new_chapters.first().index`; needed an additive path that writes an explicit `chosen_idx` inside the SAME transaction, while keeping `update_book_source_tx` + its fault-injection variant behaviorally unchanged for int1-int4.
+- Options: (1) add a `chosen_idx: Option<i64>` parameter to the existing fn (breaking signature for all callers, incl. tests); (2) additive `update_book_source_tx_at(..., chosen_idx)` that both `update_book_source_tx` and `update_book_source_tx_with_fault` delegate into (passing `first_idx` as `chosen_idx` for the unchanged-behavior wrapper).
