+- Situation: Item C — need a pure fold post-pass over `Vec<HitOrStatus>`, plus a shared display helper `draw()` must call for both single- and multi-source rows.
+- Options: (1) fold at the UI layer (in `draw()`) using a temp `HashMap`, re-deriving `HitOrStatus::Hit` fields defensively every render; (2) fold once, inside `assemble_rows`, producing a new `HitOrStatus::FoldedHit` variant that persists in `SearchState::Results.rows`.
