+# CONTRACT — legado-parity three items (delta over EXPERIMENT-BRIEF.md)
+
+## 目標
+Fix the `&` self-selector, add best-effort progress migration on switch-source, and fold duplicate cross-source search hits — each behind a pure, real-call-path-pinned helper, with zero new warnings.
+
+## 驗收條文 (sharpened; brief A1–C6 assumed, deltas + traps only)
+- **A (rule `&`)**: In `extract_within`/`select_within`/`extract_doc`/`select_nodes`/`extract_all_doc`, guard the `alt.selector == "&"` self-branch BEFORE `Selector::parse` runs, per-alt inside the loop. PROHIBITED: calling `Selector::parse("&")` on any path (it errors `EmptySelector` — that IS the bug). A1–A3: self-branch feeds the alt's accessor+replace (text default, `@attr`/`html`/`outerHtml`, `##re##rep`). A4: `&` resolves per-alt in any `||` position. A5: `select_within(el,"&")` → `vec![el]`. A7: document-level `&` → `doc.root_element()`, never error.
+- **B (migration)**: OLD name resolved by scanning old TOC for the `ChapterMeta` whose `.index == progress.chapter_index` — PROHIBITED: `old_toc[chapter_index]` (idx is non-dense). Missing progress row / no old name / no match → reset SUCCESS path (`chapter_index = toc.first().index`, `scroll_offset = 0`) — NOT a 6th abort class; the five pre-tx abort classes stay untouched. On match: `chapter_index = matched ChapterMeta.index` (PROHIBITED: matched position or `0`). The chosen idx is written INSIDE the existing single transaction (progress step 4) — PROHIBITED: any second transaction or progress write outside the tx. Preferred ripple: additive dao signature (`update_book_source_tx` delegates to `…_at(chosen_idx)`) so `int1`–`int4` + fault-injection dao tests stay green unchanged.
+- **B precedence (spec-gap resolved — log it)**: single ascending-idx pass; tier priority `a`(exact) > `b`(all-Unicode-whitespace-stripped equal) > `c`(chapter-number token equal); within the winning tier smallest idx wins. Track best `(tier, idx)` across the scan — an exact match anywhere beats a whitespace-only match earlier.
+- **B token rule (c)**: BOTH names must yield a token via the regex AND the tokens must be equal. PROHIBITED: two no-token names counting as a match; mapping Chinese numerals to Arabic (full-width→half-width Arabic normalization ONLY; cross-numeral matching is bonus, not done).
+- **B message (B6)**: PROHIBITED — any number derived from a chapter idx (`idx+1`, positions) in user-facing switch text. Migrated uses the matched chapter NAME verbatim. Exact clauses (see Constants). `SwitchOutcome` distinguishes migrated vs reset and carries matched name+idx when migrated.
+- **C (fold)**: KEY = `(name.trim(), author.as_deref().map(str::trim).unwrap_or(""))` — `None` and `Some("")` collapse together (C2 depends inversely). Order-preserving: a collapsed row sits at its FIRST occurrence's slot; later duplicate Hit rows are removed; `StatusLine` rows keep position relative to surviving rows (C5 test MUST interleave a StatusLine between two duplicates). C4: Enter on a collapsed row acts on the FIRST source's hit (first-seen order). Fold lives in a pure helper (post-pass over `Vec<HitOrStatus>` or inside `assemble_rows`).
+
+## 錯不起的表面 (surface → exact format → required pinning test)
+- CLI switch success (`handlers/switch_source.rs` `println!`) → `✓ 已換源 #{id} 至 {book_url}，{CLAUSE}` where `{CLAUSE}` comes from the shared helper → unit-test the shared helper on both migrated+reset outcomes.
+- TUI switch toast (`handlers/tui/switch_source.rs` success `Transition`) → `✓ 已換源至 {source_url}，{CLAUSE}` — same `{CLAUSE}` from the SAME shared helper (ONE helper, both paths). Pin: test asserts both call sites embed the helper output (not a re-implemented string).
+- Switch error (both paths) → `換源失敗：{anyhow chain}` — unchanged; keep zh-TW `with_context` prefixes.
+- Search row render (`handlers/tui/search.rs` `draw`) → single-source `{name} / {author|-} [{src}]`; collapsed `{name} - {author|-} [{n}源: {s1}, {s2}, …]` — MUST be produced by a pure display helper that `draw()` calls; unit-test that helper on count==1 and count≥2 (test pins the helper the real UI calls, not a copy).
+- StatusLine rows (`assemble_rows`) → `源 {name}：錯誤 {msg}` / `源 {name}：逾時` / `源 {name} 未查（時間預算用盡）` — unchanged; C6 tests assert they survive folding in place.
+
+## Verbatim Constants
+```
+# B — chapter-number regex (first capture group), full-width→half-width Arabic normalize, compare as strings
+第\s*([0-9０-９一二三四五六七八九十百千零〇两兩]+)\s*[章回節节卷]
+
+# B — SwitchOutcome shared-helper clauses (exact; no idx-derived number)
+migrated: 進度已遷移：{matched_name}      # e.g. 進度已遷移：第12章 風起
+reset:    進度重置到首章
+
+# C — search row display (author_display = author.trim() if non-empty else "-")
+single : {name} / {author_display} [{source_name}]
+folded : {name} - {author_display} [{count}源: {name1}, {name2}, ...]
+
+# Global: introduce NO new warnings; the two pre-existing dead_code warnings must remain exactly two.
+```
